Hello to everyone reading this! This is something I wanted to share with you and anybody who wants to go out and follow their goals. I firmly believe that with any new project one should challenge themselves to go a little bit further than the last. This is how progress is made. So here is what I learned from Be A Rock:

1) How to create massive landscapes;


2) How to fine tune, how to texture how to populate them;


3) How to make them beautiful and interesting;


4) How to work with lighting - that was a difficult one, light is very tricky to get right, still learning;


5) Pacing and story telling for games;


6) How to work with voice actors - how to hire, build relationships, give feedback 6) How to create a game concept, research and write a script;

7) How to design challenging puzzles;

Thanks for reading!
- Theseus Games

Thank you to everyone for your wonderful feedback! Here are the improvements for version 1.2:
- Xbox controller support added;
- Guiding tokens counter added at the end of each level;
- Level design tweaks on every map for better player experience;
- Updated cinematics;
- Rock buddy improved A.I.; 
- Puzzle improvements and bug fixes;
- Player messages in Epilogue level added;
- Minor glitches removed;
